  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts as an Aura3D orrery. It passes typecheck, but I couldn't run or render it here. The lighting, the ring orientation and the framing are untested.\n\n- **Star and planets:** a glowing emissive star sits at the centre with a point light, and there are five planets in different sizes and colours. They orbit at radii from 2.6 to 8.5 and at different speeds, and each orbit is slightly inclined. A dim torus draws each orbit path.\n- **Ring:** the fourth planet (\"saturno\") has a flattened torus ring, tilted and moved with the planet every frame. I assumed the torus lies in the XY plane, as its geometry code suggests, and rotated it flat from there. If the ring looks wrong, check that rotation first.\n- **Look:** the background is near-black (#02030a), with a faint neutral environment light so the planets' dark sides stay visible. `effects.bloom` gives the star its glow.\n- **Motion and camera:** the planets move every frame from `f.time`, so frames differ. The camera is perspective at (0, 13, 15.5), looking at the origin with fov 46. By my arithmetic it should frame the outermost orbit, but I didn't check it visually.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nThe point light's intensity (900) and distance (60) are guesses. If the planets render too dark or too bright, adjust those first.\n\n",
